==English==
{{was wotd|2009|April|29}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|crochety}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|crotchet|y}}, using {{m|en|crotchet}} in the 16th-century sense of a [[whim]] or [[fancy]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkɹɒtʃ.ə.tɪ/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkɹɑ.t͡ʃɪ.ti/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-crotchety.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# [[cranky|Cranky]], [[disagreeable]], or [[stubborn]], especially if prone to [[odd]] [[whim]]s or [[fancy|fancies]].
#* {{RQ:Faulkner Sound and Fury|page=184|text=He wouldnt even let old Wilkie touch it do you remember Gerald but always gathered it himself and made his own julep. He was as '''crochety''' about his julep as an old maid, measuring everything by a recipe in his head.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Andrew Anthony|title=David Mitchell: ‘I have no reason to have these apocalyptic musings’|work=The Observer|date=2019-11-03|url=https://www.theguardian.com/media/2019/nov/03/david-mitchell-interview-apocalyptic-musings-dishonesty-is-the-second-best-policy|issn=0029-7712|passage=He has a happy home life, two sitcoms on the go and a new book in the offing. So why is the comedian, actor and Observer columnist still so '''crotchety'''?}}

